    "created_at": "2024-01-27T23:49:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-27T23:50:05Z",
    "body": "> Is this behavior currently overridable by websites in Gecko? Just wondering whether `!important` is appropriate here in the UA style.\r\n\r\nI don't think it's overridable by websites in Gecko, and conceptually I don't think it should be either, so I'd say `!important` is appropriate and it should help simplify simulating the behavior with custom code.",
